  "term": "anomaly",
  "definition": "In historical psychology, a mental anomaly is a clear departure from what is considered typical or normal in mental abilities or functioning. It refers to an unusual or exceptional irregularity and can describe traits or symptoms discussed in abnormal psychology.",
